estMigrationBehavior` should also be in the…"],["5136e50f_2a605ad6",36,-4,1,"Can we include a bit of a comment in this code as to what the expected format is? I find it a bit confusing that we are attempting to read the id as a string and below we are attempting to read it as…"],["54e45243_9fef4ae2",36,-4,1,"Why not use the `GetType()` method to ensure the expected type is present and then proceed parsing based on it?"],["606d1772_a638d7e7",36,-4,1,"A note on why `NoRestrictions` is ok to use here will be useful."],["9bc78fcf_0c6dcf63",36,-4,1,"This checks the `id` for empty and ignores it, while the `AsString` branch above does not check for empty string."],["f8674c01_4a8517e1",36,-4,0,"This method returns nullptr while the parser for `migrate_from` always returns a value. Is this inconsistency intentional?"]],0,1381],[7253635,20439,224,4.195,3.394,[[1,0.867,137,196],[27,0.116,54,25],[20,0.017,81,3]],[["6f458125_6ab25604",40,-5,1,"What's the advantage of having this C++ class? Can we instead reuse `proto::WebAppMigrationSource` as the data type to store in the web_app.cc class? That way, serialization/deserialization and…"],["97862a24_e2b61c30",41,-5,1,"nit: Might be nicer to break down into 2 different error enums, `kInvalidWebAppUnvalidatedMigrationSource` and `kInvalidWebAppValidatedMigrationSource` so that in case of errors, we can pinpoint…"]],0,1382],[7219588,20439,534,10.952,8.912,[[1,0.789,138,423],[53,0.211,0,113]],[["4b571a86_81c029df",42,-1,0,"should we CHECK that this url is_valid()?"],["7090284d_5cf28367",42,-1,1,"nit: type"]],0,1383],[7269382,20440,26,0.721,0.543,[[1,139]],[],0,1384],[4092882,20440,1,0.075,0.04,[[5,4]],[],0,1385],[7275616,20440,35,1.326,1.047,[[0,0.684,252,24],[54,0.316,12,11]],[["3f6b193e_65e5ee44",43,0,0,"Interesting! Seems like this will only be called in the beginning of the test, do we have to worry about potential `about:blank` tabs also appearing in the middle of test execution? Seems like…"]],0,1386]]}